From 4cf1d8d145b1c57938d2e27328de3806d6046fa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ThreeMuskets12 <23061574+ThreeMuskets12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:51:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] GraphiteOS: color e-ink look for the built-in display

The built-in display is fully GPU composited and the composited frame is run through an e-ink
shader (warm paper tone, desaturated, ~300 colors, 2px ordered dither). A new frame is only shown
every 1/15 s; frames in between repeat the last filtered frame. SurfaceFlinger still latches,
releases and presents every frame as normal, so apps see normal frame pacing.

The filter is skipped while photo or camera apps, camera buffers, protected content, or video
from a calling app are visible. Screenshots, virtual displays and external displays are never
filtered. adb shell service call SurfaceFlinger 1999 i32 <0|1> turns the filter off or on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
